      ],
      "gap": "The construction or argument and the full treatment promised by the declared status (proved=annex:p15.model-density-invariance) are not supplied for every case the entry states. The theorem asserts at body lines 136-137 that declaring a new flat prior in new parameter coordinates is not, in general, a transport of the prior. annex:p15.model-density-invariance (annex lines 97-104) proves only invariance of m_k under the stated transport. It then disclaims the other case ('not under an arbitrary reassignment of a coordinate density') without a counterexample or argument. The chapter also gives no worked boundary for the coordinate part; the only worked boundary, at body lines 148-155, covers density versions. The failure condition 'Missing promised direction/case' therefore holds for this entry. A uniform-theta versus uniform-theta^2 example exists in thm:p15-bayes-transformation (bayesian-updating-prediction.tex lines 314-319), but neither this theorem nor its proof cites it, and that example concerns posterior means, not the marginal likelihood m_k. All other parts of the entry have written proofs: likelihood versions, intrinsic Radon-Nikodym form, change of reference density, and observation bijection."
